---
/*
 * I tre punti di forza (spec della home, §3.2): una fascia tipografica, non tre schede uguali. Il titolo è quello di
 * «What you get»; sotto la fascia, i testi delle sue tre schede, parola per parola, senza riquadri.
 */
---
<section class="h-sec wrap" aria-labelledby="h-band-title">
  <h2 id="h-band-title">Everything runs on Discord's own interface.</h2>
  <div class="h-pillars">
    <div class="h-pillar">
      <h3>Simple to use</h3>
      <p>One command to remember. Everything else is a Discord button with a familiar icon, built to take the fewest clicks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="h-pillar">
      <h3>Packed with features</h3>
      <p>Owners and tags, reminders, groups and subtasks, webhooks, a timeline of every change. In English, Italian, German, French, Spanish and Portuguese.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="h-pillar">
      <h3>Two ways to work</h3>
      <p>Tick tasks off right in the channel, or open the list in the Activity and work on it together, live.</p>
      <a class="h-link" href="#two-ways">See the two ways</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ul class="h-feats" role="list">
    <li>
      <img src="/icons/task_list.png" alt="" />
      <div>
        <h3>Shared lists</h3>
        <p>Create a checklist from plain text. One line per task, starting with a dash; a few spaces before the dash make a subtask. Groups are recognized automatically.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <img src="/icons/owner.png" alt="" />
      <div>
        <h3>Owners &amp; tags</h3>
        <p>Give each task an owner and tag the people or roles to notify &mdash; right on the task, not in a side conversation.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <img src="/icons/alertW.png" alt="" />
      <div>
        <h3>Reminders</h3>
        <p>Attach a reminder with a start date and a time zone &mdash; and, on Premium, repetitions. TTM remembers so you don't have to.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
